Field guidance:
- historical_evidence and failed_approaches: only records returned by a tool, with the status as recorded; empty lists
  if nothing relevant was returned.
- testability.p_testable: probability that the question can be answered with the stated data at useful statistical power.
- prior_work.already_answered: whether retrieved earlier work already answered substantially the same question.
  Use "unknown" if no earlier work was retrieved. List identifiers you relied on in prior_work.cited.
- predicted_outcome: probabilities (summing to 1) of what a competent test of the question as posed would conclude:
  supported, rejected (adequately powered null), untestable (cannot be tested with this data), artifact (apparent
  effect produced by a flaw), uncertain (inconclusive or inadequately tested).
- decision: proceed, proceed_with_changes (state the changes in design), or do_not_proceed.
- design: a pre-registration-quality plan even if the decision is do_not_proceed (then describe the minimum viable test).

{
 "research_concepts": ["player absence", "offensive reorganization relative to baseline L", "change in points per possession", "play-type possession records", "substitution rotation intervals", "lineup spells"],
 "methodological_questions": [
  "Is 'reorganization relative to L' defined operationally, and what is L?",
  "Is the reorganization metric computed independently of the PPP outcome, or derived from the same possessions?",
  "What is the minimum detectable association with 148 spells, and does the stated MDE (rho) match that calculation?",
  "How are selection into absence, usage, and opponent/period effects controlled?"
 ],
 "historical_evidence": [
  {
   "id": "FAM:SF-APPS-088",
   "status_as_recorded": "supported",
   "finding": "Offensive-identity resilience study. Connector absence displaced team offensive identity (D_A) more than usage-matched non-organizer absence: unmatched 0.2020 vs 0.1021 (t=5.97, p=2.87e-08); usage-matched paired dD_A +0.1151, P(conn>ctrl)=81.2%, t=6.35, p=7.35e-09, n=96; vs terminal +0.0777, t=2.37, p=0.0261, n=25. Recorded flags: LIM:small_sample; RISK:MECHANICAL_FLOOR; RISK:SAMPLE_SIZE_POWER."
  },
  {
   "id": "FAM:SF-APPS-075",
   "status_as_recorded": "not a hypothesis test",
   "finding": "Extended possession value. Four of eight play types show a downstream opponent next-PPP component of roughly 0.01–0.02 PPP (e.g. CUT +0.0220, TRANSITION +0.0145). DRIVE downstream not real. Most player-level downstream effects were non-significant after BH correction."
  },
  {
   "id": "FAM:SF-APPS-078",
   "status_as_recorded": "not a hypothesis test",
   "finding": "Possession ending state vs opponent points/possessions over the next 90–180s. Live turnovers raise opponent possession volume (dOppPoss +0.298) more than PPP (+0.055). Verdict recorded as descriptive; no inferential tests in the core table. Sample n=911,968."
  },
  {
   "id": "FAM:SF-APPA-005",
   "status_as_recorded": "untestable",
   "finding": "Defensive scheme change using inferred labels: within-game change 61.0%, cross-game 67.7%, transition matrices near-uniform. Doc caveat: the inferred label cannot separate real defensive adjustment from the offense executing differently. Recorded failure mechanism A_unanswerable; LIM:label_or_classification_error; RISK:LABEL_ERROR."
  }
 ],
 "failed_approaches": [
  {
   "id": "FAM:SF-APPA-005",
   "what_failed": "Testing scheme change from inferred per-possession labels",
   "why": "Recorded as untestable: the label cannot distinguish defensive adjustment from offensive variation, and near-uniform transition matrices are consistent with label noise. A reorganization metric built from inferred play labels would carry the same problem."
  },
  {
   "id": "FAM:SF-APPS-078",
   "what_failed": "Using possession-ending states as a source of downstream PPP effects",
   "why": "Recorded as descriptive with no inferential tests. The recorded live-turnover effect is mainly volume (possession count), and the record calls that effect largely definitional, so PPP-based conclusions are not established."
  },
  {
   "id": "FAM:SF-APPS-075",
   "what_failed": "Detecting player-level downstream PPP effects",
   "why": "Recorded effects are small (about 0.01–0.02 PPP) relative to direct PPP gaps, and most player-level effects were non-significant after BH correction. The record lists the mechanism as unclear."
  }
 ],
 "evidence_establishes": [
  "Usage-matched comparisons of absent organizers versus other absent players have been used in this project to show large identity-change effects (FAM:SF-APPS-088, n=96 matched pairs).",
  "Downstream and volume effects of possession outcomes are small relative to direct PPP differences (FAM:SF-APPS-075, FAM:SF-APPS-078).",
  "Inferred labels from play-by-play can be too noisy to support scheme-change conclusions (FAM:SF-APPA-005)."
 ],
 "evidence_does_not_establish": [
  "None of the retrieved records defines or tests 'offensive reorganization relative to L'. No record tests the association with change in PPP.",
  "No retrieved record estimates the association between reorganization and PPP change after absence, or the effect size of such an association.",
  "Whether the 148-spell sample is adequate for the question as posed is not established by any record. SF-APPS-088 used n=96 and flagged small-sample limits.",
  "The retrieved records do not show that the reorganization metric is reliable across seasons or teams."
 ],
 "own_inferences": [
  "The question as posed is underspecified: L, the reorganization metric, the direction of the predicted relation, and the PPP-change window are not defined.",
  "If the reorganization metric and PPP change are both derived from the same play-by-play possessions, the association may be partly mechanical.",
  "At n=148 and alpha 0.05 (two-sided), 80% power corresponds to a detectable correlation of about rho ≈ 0.23 (Fisher-z approximation, 2.8/sqrt(145)). Whether the stated 'mde rho' matches this is unclear.",
  "The SF-APPS-088 pattern (identity displacement after connector absence) suggests the reorganization signal may be concentrated in a few high-usage organizers, so a pooled association could be dominated by a small subset."
 ],
 "uncertainties": [
  "The definition and units of L, the reorganization metric, and the PPP-change window are missing from the task statement.",
  "The units line ('n=986; n=148, mde rho; 148 spells') is ambiguous as to which n is the analysis unit.",
  "Retrieval returned four records, none on this metric. A follow-up search (search_documents) was not run, so related records may exist.",
  "The 2025-26 playoffs are complete as of 2026-06-21, before the 2026-11-01 freeze date. The 2025-26 regular season is complete from 2026-04-13. Both are usable; the freeze date should still be pinned."
 ],
 "historical_effect": {
  "changed_decision": "yes",
  "explanation": "The retrieved records support a unit-matched design (usage-matched absences, as in SF-APPS-088). They also show that inferred labels (SF-APPA-005) and downstream or volume-based PPP metrics (SF-APPS-075, SF-APPS-078) produce weak or untestable results. These points led to a proceed_with_changes decision: the metric must be defined and validated before the test, and the test must control for usage and match on absence type. The records do not test the question itself, so they do not on their own make the question answerable."
 },
