  "estimand": "Standardized association (partial correlation or slope, with CI) between offensive reorganization relative to a pre-absence baseline L and the change in team PPP from pre- to post-absence, conditional on usage and opponent controls.",
  "unit": "Team-level absence spell (one row per absence episode of a rotation player), not per possession.",
  "sample": "All complete regular-season and playoff spells from 2022-23 through 2025-26 (2025-26 regular season complete from 2026-04-13; 2025-26 playoffs complete from 2026-06-21). Freeze the data version at 2026-11-01. The 148-spell count should be checked against this definition.",
  "power": "At n=148 and alpha 0.05 two-sided, 80% power detects rho ≈ 0.23. Report the achieved MDE for the final sample; the stated 'mde rho' must be reconciled with this figure before analysis.",
  "controls": "Pre-absence baseline L computed only from data before the absence (no lookahead). Usage-matched controls (absent non-organizers, per FAM:SF-APPS-088). Adjust for opponent strength, minutes, and season. Validate the reorganization metric's reliability across two split halves before use. Use reorganization labels not derived from the outcome window where possible.",
  "falsification": "Placebo outcome: change in PPP for non-absence windows of the same teams. Placebo exposure: reorganization computed for randomly chosen spells with no absence. Expect near-zero association for both. A positive placebo association indicates mechanical or confounded structure.",
  "multiplicity": "Pre-register one primary definition of L and reorganization and one PPP window. Treat other definitions as secondary with Holm or BH correction.",
  "decision_rule": "Primary: support only if the pre-registered partial association is positive with a 95% CI excluding zero and the usage-matched and placebo checks pass. Reject if the CI covers zero with the achieved MDE below the expected effect size. Otherwise report as uncertain. Do not claim mechanism from association alone.",
